{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"852741576237121561","content":"Ivaela guides <@860303482065256448>  over to the first of the statues, which depicts a drider woman with red legs and a large swollen abdomen. \"This is Lolth. Patron deity of the Drow and known as The Demon Queen of Spiders, Queen of Darkness, and Dark Mother, among others.\" She continues on to the second statue, which depicts a large spider sitting upright and weaving. \"This is Anansi, trickster god, teacher, weaver of stories and bringer of light and dark.\" She continues to the last large statue, which depicts what appears to be an elven-looking humanoid with six arms. \"And this is Web. They are the most recent to rise to prominence here but they have a solid following. They are god of family, sewers, and curiosity, and known as 'Parriarch'.\"","created_at":"2021-07-17T23:06:03.794000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"866093425153540127","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
